# Git Commit Standards

## Format

```
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

<body>

<footer>
```

## Types

| Type | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `feat` | New feature |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `style` | Formatting, no code change |
| `refactor` | Code restructuring |
| `test` | Adding/updating tests |
| `chore` | Maintenance, deps |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `ci` | CI/CD changes |
| `revert` | Revert previous commit |

## Examples

### Feature
```
feat(auth): add JWT token refresh

Implement automatic token refresh 5 minutes before expiration.
Stores refresh token in httpOnly cookie.

Closes #123
```

### Bug Fix
```
fix(api): resolve race condition in order processing

Add mutex lock to prevent concurrent order modifications.
Fixes intermittent 500 errors on checkout.
```

### Refactor
```
refactor(user-service): extract validation logic

Move validation to separate module for reuse.
No behavior changes.
```

## Rules

- Subject line: max 50 characters
- Body: wrap at 72 characters
- Use imperative mood ("add" not "added")
- No period at end of subject
- Reference issues: `Closes #123`, `Fixes #456`
